                <pb facs="0451" n="377" xml:id="pg377"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Clay to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 24, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> It becomes my painful duty to inform you
                    that this morning at half-past twelve o’clock his Imperial Highness the Grand
                    Duke Héritier died at Nice, of a diseased spine, under which he had been
                    gradually sinking. His Majesty the Emperor of Russia and her Royal Highness the
                    Princess Dagmar, of Denmark, his affianced bride, got to Nice in time to witness
                    the last hours of this amiable but ill-fated youth. All Russia, the diplomatic
                    corps, and every one who knew this interesting young man, lament most sincerely
                    his untimely end. For my self I had added to the respect which I owed him as the
                    heir of a great throne and the son of a noble father, the friendship which his
                    amiability and many virtues inspired. * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. M. CLAY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. H. Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
